1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
Kieran: So Jane - you'll be off to Denmark soon to do your work placement.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,780
Jane: Yes, I'm really looking forward to it

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:11,120
and I've just started packing up all my books to put in storage.

4
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:13,510
Kieran: Well, I hope they don't get spoilt.

5
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:19,080
Jane: It's OK - my grandfather works in a bookshop and he told me how to pack them.

6
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,730
Kieran: Oh, that's helpful.

7
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:26,270
Jane: He says you have to support the spine otherwise the paper can come away from the cover.

8
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:28,080
Kieran: Yeah - that's obvious.

9
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:31,400
Jane: He also told me to pack them flat in the box

10
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:34,881
not on their side - again because they can bend

11
00:00:34,881 --> 00:00:37,960
and if you leave them like that for, say

12
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,330
a year, it's quite hard to get them back to their normal shape.

13
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:44,674
Kieran: Well, it's pretty clear that ruins them,

14
00:00:44,674 --> 00:00:48,320
but a lot of people just can't be bothered to protect their books.

15
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:53,490
Jane: He always says it's such a shame that publishers don't use better-quality paper.

16
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:56,840
Kieran: It's the acid in the paper that causes the problem, isn't it?

17
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:59,878
Jane: Yeah - that's why old books go yellow.

18
00:00:59,878 --> 00:01:04,940
You know some of the books my grandfather's given me are like that already.

19
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:05,710
Kieran: Oh...

20
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:09,440
Jane: I should dump them really if they're going to deteriorate further

21
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:11,459
but I'd feel bad.

22
00:01:11,459 --> 00:01:15,930
They'll always remind me of him. He's quite a collector, you know.

23
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:17,630
Kieran: Well, if they're important to you...

24
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:20,980
Jane: Yeah - I'd regret just throwing them away.

25
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:25,002
Kieran: You know, maybe it's because I was taught to treasure books.

26
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:28,406
but I hate seeing students force open the pages - of paperbacks.

27
00:01:28,406 --> 00:01:31,500
They press so hard they end up breaking the spine.

28
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:39,030
Jane: I know, but unfortunately, paperbacks aren't designed to last a long time and people know that.

29
00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:41,540
Hardbacks aren't quite as weak.

30
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:43,240
Kieran: Yeah, they're different, I suppose

31
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:47,840
But I still don't think people value hardbacks like they used to.

32
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:52,053
Jane: Well, they aren't decorative, are they, like other objects.

33
00:01:52,053 --> 00:01:58,180
Plus, nowadays, people don't keep them out on shelves as much as they used to.

34
00:01:58,180 --> 00:01:59,837
Kieran: That's such a pity.

35
00:01:59,837 --> 00:02:02,360
When I visit someone - if they have, say

36
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:06,190
a colourful book on a table, it's the first thing I'm drawn to.

37
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:14,410
Jane: I agree - and book covers can be a work of art in themselves. Some are really eye-catching.

38
00:02:14,410 --> 00:02:17,229
Kieran: I've always been taught to handle books carefully.

39
00:02:17,229 --> 00:02:21,740
If you watch someone take a book off a shelf, well, they usually do it wrong.

40
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:27,609
Jane: Ah, my grandfather says, you should put your hand right over the top of the book.

41
00:02:27,609 --> 00:02:29,900
or if you can't do that

42
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:35,550
pull the other books on the shelf aside so that you can hold the whole cover.

43
00:02:35,550 --> 00:02:37,210
Kieran: When did you learn all this?

44
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:41,160
Jane: He watched me pull a heavy book off the shelf when I was small

45
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:44,450
and it fell on the floor and broke apart.

46
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:45,010
Kieran: Oh dear!

47
00:02:45,010 --> 00:02:47,710
Jane: I can still remember it!

48
00:02:47,710 --> 00:02:49,460
Kieran: You know what I really like?

49
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:50,030
Jane: What?

50
00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:51,940
Kieran: The smell of new books.

51
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,100
Jane: Me too.

52
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,300
Kieran: My parents used to laugh at me when I was a kid

53
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,176
because I loved putting books up to my nose.

54
00:02:58,176 --> 00:02:59,560
Almost as much as reading them!

55
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:02,360
Jane: New books aren't cheap, though, are they?

56
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,360
Kieran: I guess we're lucky we can buy them.

57
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:08,220
Jane: My grandfather stocks second-hand books as well as new ones

58
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:11,160
and they don't smell quite as good.

59
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:15,710
Kieran: I'd love to have a bookshop like your grandfather. What's it like?

60
00:03:15,710 --> 00:03:20,860
Jane: Well, it's quite big - it's got two floors and an attic

61
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:24,320
and he stocks all kinds of books really.

62
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:28,170
Kieran: I guess he treasures things like first editions and other rare books.

63
00:03:28,170 --> 00:03:32,700
Jane: Yeah - you might think he'd keep those in the attic or somewhere.

64
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:34,150
Kieran:... so they'd be hidden?

65
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:37,894
Jane: Yeah. But he likes people to know that he has them.

66
00:03:37,894 --> 00:03:43,510
So, he puts them out in the shop but makes sure you need a ladder to get them.

67
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:45,530
Kieran: Right. That would prevent any thefts!

68
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:46,580
Jane: Uhuh.

69
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:48,350
Kieran: Does he stock books for children?

70
00:03:48,350 --> 00:03:52,177
Jane: He does. He particularly likes to encourage kids to read;

71
00:03:52,177 --> 00:04:00,180
he always says that he used to sit under the stairs as a child with a pile of books and read them all.

72
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:01,570
Kieran: Is that where he keeps them, then?

73
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:06,494
Jane: Not exactly - he's got a dedicated area on the ground floor

74
00:04:06,494 --> 00:04:09,860
with cushions so that parents can enter with their toddlers

75
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:13,690
go there and spend some time reading to them.

76
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:14,650
Kieran: Oh cool.

77
00:04:14,650 --> 00:04:17,660
Jane: And then there's a place for pushchairs by the front door

78
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:21,130
And a café if anyone needs refreshments.

79
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:22,180
Kieran: That's good to know.

80
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:27,830
Jane: As I said, it's a big shop and there's a storage area out the back as well.

81
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:31,560
Kieran: Oh, what does he keep there? Books he wants to throw away?

82
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:34,196
Jane: He hardly ever throws anything away -

83
00:04:34,196 --> 00:04:39,090
he just leaves unwanted books by the front door for customers to take.

84
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:40,840
Kieran: Well, that's very nice.

85
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:45,060
Jane: Yeah - and books people or institutions have requested

86
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,970
they all go at the far end.

87
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:48,790
Kieran: Oh.

88
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:54,350
Jane: He thinks it's best to keep these out of the main shopping area as they're boxed and new.

89
00:04:54,350 --> 00:04:56,450
Kieran: Did you get your coursebooks from him?

90
00:04:56,450 --> 00:05:00,480
Jane: Naturally. He stocks books for a lot of the colleges

91
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,707
He used to keep these books on the first floor,

92
00:05:03,707 --> 00:05:06,800
but now there's a new university in my hometown

93
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:10,272
he's moved them downstairs to attract the students.

94
00:05:10,272 --> 00:05:15,110
They're actually part of the coffee shop, on low shelves all around it.

95
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:18,420
Kieran: Pretty central then. You'll have to take me there some time!
